Resume bound Datalog sessions with certified partial models (#668)

Expose bound Datalog continuations and certified partial models

Retain native rule, round, ordered publication and stratum progress across
resource or stop refusals. EvaluationSession and complete-only evaluation use
the same execution owners. Raising a cumulative allowance resumes the original
work without replaying successful joins or guard calls.

Require explicit canonical snapshot, guard-semantics and evidence-regime
identities alongside the authored-program digest. Resume rejects a changed
binding or derivation mode before work; original source and guard failures stay
typed terminal failures. PartialModel exposes published certified facts,
independently checkable recorded derivations and complete/lower-bound/withheld
stratum status. Only completion permits taking an Evaluation. Runtime handles
never enter the partial identity.

Update the English and Chinese book together and correct the reviewed
authored-program translation. The host-adapted StopSignal contract now agrees
with the implementation.

Validation: 429 native library tests, 46 integration cases, one doctest and all
31 public Node/WASM runtime cases pass. Controls cover every pause cut,
one-credit resumption, all five governors, changed bindings, source/guard
failures, negative dependencies, exact final work/proofs and original wide
handles. Strict all-target Clippy, warnings-denied rustdoc, entailment consumer
compilation, helper hygiene and normal commit/push hooks pass. Full translation
qualification passes all six rendering gates, all 26 translated SPARQL fences
and 3,377 translated messages without drift.

Final-head CI 39550566827, Docs 39550566832 and PR-wide checks pass. Independent
source/documentation review has no unresolved actionable finding after the
translation fix. The docstring heuristic identifies no public contract defect;
strict public docs pass. No human approval or independent runtime execution is
claimed. The assessed integration is clean; the base-only Python dependency
repair is covered by passing main qualification. No CI waiver.

Closes #667.

Broader Datalog, memory and proof parent contracts remain open: chase,
entailment partial closures, governed SPARQL pages, common admission/spill and
reusable proof-query/revision work are not completed by this delivery.

